{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1297008-qlippothic-spheres-and-non-nephandi","id":1297008,"title":"Qlippothic Spheres and non-Nephandi?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-15T09:43:55-07:00","id":1297008,"title":"Qlippothic Spheres and non-Nephandi?","content":"So the wiki entry on Qlippothic spheres (<a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Qlippothic_Sphere\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Qlippothic_Sphere</a>) has an odd line that suggests that some non-nephandi occasionally utilize qlippothic magic. Does anyone know if this has been demonstrated (or disproven) anywhere? And what are the implications of a non-fallen using that kind of magic with a normal avatar?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T10:55:15-07:00","id":1297030,"title":"","content":"I feel this depends on the degree to which Nephandus is a sign of allegiance vs a descriptor. A Technocrat is a member of the Technocratic Union but there are technomancers outside of its walls. Magick based on negation or fraying the walls of reality could be Qlippothic without someone being a formal member of a sect. There are probably &quot;orphan&quot; infernalists, malfeans, and worshippers of the outer things that could use something that would certainly look like Qlippothic magic without being a member of one of the formal Nephandi groups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-15T20:29:34-07:00","id":1297132,"title":"","content":"The thing about Sphere variants, whether they're Technocratic or Qlippothic, is that they're also Focus-dependent: Data requires that you at least somewhat believe that Everything is Data; Dimensional Science requires that you accept something akin to Tychoidean Cosmology; Primal Utility requires that you buy into Hypereconomics; and the Qlippothic Spheres require you to have the sort of mindset that the Nephandi have. This replaces earlier editions' notions of certain Sphere variants belonging to certain groups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 07-02-2019, 03:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T03:02:43-07:00","id":1297188,"title":"","content":"Gonna agree with Dataweaver here. A Mage who can employ Qlippothic Spheres is one who has jumped onto the particular, antithetical mindset that Nephandi operate under as a matter of course.<br /> <br /> Indeed, one could argue that beginning to think like a Nephandus indicates that one has taken the first step towards going through a &quot;Caul in one's heart&quot;. The sort of auto-Fall that requires no physical Caul (personally, I'm of the opinion that the first Nephandi all went through a &quot;Caul of the heart&quot;, in the pre-history days before the first physical Cauls were built to expedite the Fall).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T06:07:57-07:00","id":1297221,"title":"","content":"Every reference I've found has tied the Qlippothic spheres directly to being a full Nephandi. Though personally I prefer Dataweaver and Bluecho's take.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T10:18:55-07:00","id":1297286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1297008-qlippothic-spheres-and-non-nephandi?p=1297188#post1297188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gonna agree with Dataweaver here. A Mage who can employ Qlippothic Spheres is one who has jumped onto the particular, antithetical mindset that Nephandi operate under as a matter of course.<br /> <br /> Indeed, one could argue that beginning to think like a Nephandus indicates that one has taken the first step towards going through a &quot;Caul in one's heart&quot;. The sort of auto-Fall that requires no physical Caul (personally, I'm of the opinion that the first Nephandi all went through a &quot;Caul of the heart&quot;, in the pre-history days before the first physical Cauls were built to expedite the Fall).</div> </div> </div> </div>Really agree with this idea of the Caul being personal and internal.<br /> <br /> For me, the Cauls are reached during disastrous Quiets and Seekings, but only if the Mage in question is suitably Nephandic. You can be guided there by a mentor (this is the most common way), but if you are especially suited to inversion and descent then you will find your way there naturally... of course you will have the choice to not take the plunge.<br /> <br /> I prefer this because it makes Nephandi a tad more... universal within the Mage experience. You could eradicate every single Nephandus and they'd still return, because becoming a Nephandus isn't some Special Dark Ritual (although it can be), it's simply a person making a really terrible choice. This brings it a bit more in line with the idea of becoming a Marauder, also; all of these sad and dark paths are technically available to all Mages, they're just exceptionally rare. The Widderslainte often find their way to the Cauls when they Awaken, and if they don't (or refuse) then they will find themselves back there as they perform Seekings and enter Quiets.<br /> <br /> As for how Nephandi find eachother, I like them to have the ability to notice eachother instinctively with the Awareness trait.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T10:46:51-07:00","id":1297293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1297008-qlippothic-spheres-and-non-nephandi?p=1297221#post1297221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every reference I've found has tied the Qlippothic spheres directly to being a full Nephandi. Though personally I prefer Dataweaver and Bluecho's take.</div> </div> </div> </div>Every reference to date comes from a pre-M20 edition, where faction was used as <i>the</i> determiner of paradigm. Mad scientist? You must be an Etherite. Witch? You're a Verbena. And so on. In that context, it makes sense to tie the Qlippothic Spheres directly to the Nephandi. <br /> <br /> But with M20 taking pains to decouple Focus from faction (in the sense that while every faction has a Focus, not everyone with that Focus belongs to that faction), I won't be surprised if <b>Book of the Fallen</b> opens the door a bit and presents the Qlippothic Spheres as something anyone with a suitable warped mindset can take. It's just that, by their nature, all Nephandi have that suitably warped mindset.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 07-02-2019, 02:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T10:52:33-07:00","id":1297294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1297008-qlippothic-spheres-and-non-nephandi?p=1297293#post1297293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every reference to date comes from a pre-M20 edition, where faction was used as <i>the</i> determiner of paradigm.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're in M20, p. 232.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T14:17:29-07:00","id":1297354,"title":"","content":"Fair enough. The full extent of what M20 says about them is \u201cin game terms, they're exactly the same as the regular Spheres.\u201d This isn't <i>quite</i> true of the MRev Qlippothic Spheres; but it's really close (and the mechanical differences aren't <i>clearly</i> spelled out; they're just vaguely described along the lines of \u201cthis Sphere has a harder time doing this rather than that\u201d), and I'm perfectly fine with M20 going all out on this point \u2014 which renders moot the question of who can have them. <br /> <br /> But even if <b>Book of the Fallen</b> changes that and we end up with actual mechanical differences, I still say that they're gated by some combination of paradigm and practice, not by one's allegiance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-16T17:28:56-07:00","id":1297396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1297008-qlippothic-spheres-and-non-nephandi?p=1297354#post1297354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair enough. The full extent of what M20 says about them is \u201cin game terms, they're exactly the same as the regular Spheres.\u201d This isn't <i>quite</i> true of the MRev Qlippothic Spheres; but it's really close (and the mechanical differences aren't <i>clearly</i> spelled out; they're just vaguely described along the lines of \u201cthis Sphere has a harder time doing this rather than that\u201d), and I'm perfectly fine with M20 going all out on this point \u2014 which renders moot the question of who can have them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you read the 1e Book of Madness? It gives a single Qlippothic Entropy sphere which looks a lot like a precursor to the way the Technocratic spheres work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But even if <b>Book of the Fallen</b> changes that and we end up with actual mechanical differences, I still say that they're gated by some combination of paradigm and practice, not by one's allegiance. </div> </div> </div>It's not allegiance as such, it's going through the Cauls that gives you access to the Qlippothic spheres. For that reason I kinda suspect BotF probably won't alter it that much. Though, again, I prefer the version you're outlining.<br /> <br /> I mean, I personally think the Nephandi actually suffer from a lot of legacy baggage, the Cauls first among them. I dunno about everyone else but the idea of the Masters of the Traditions and Technocracy becoming so fixated on the Ascension War that they start to descend is interesting in a way that the same people dancing round Cthulhu just isn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T02:28:09-07:00","id":1297668,"title":"","content":"I really never liked the whole &quot;qlippothic stuff is always yucky and evil&quot; angle.<br /> I mean there's a lot of real life occult groups that do qlippothic stuff, allegedly work with or even worship spirits considered demons, or with Cthulu. It would be cool to be able to draw inspiration from them without feeling like I'm breaking canon by not having every mage with a tysonomicon or a red card be a nephandus or on their way to becoming one, that's all I'm saying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":20546,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20546-dragonchild","user":"Dragonchild","date":". 03-18-2019, 05:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20546-dragonchild","name":"Dragonchild","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-18T06:40:32-07:00","id":1297706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragonchild</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1297008-qlippothic-spheres-and-non-nephandi?p=1297668#post1297668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean there's a lot of real life occult groups that do qlippothic stuff, allegedly work with or even worship spirits considered demons, or with Cthulu. It would be cool to be able to draw inspiration from them without feeling like I'm breaking canon by not having every mage with a tysonomicon or a red card be a nephandus or on their way to becoming one, that's all I'm saying.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's using Qlippothic as a interesting label to talk about something. If you want to have a Hermetic or whoever to use the actual Qlippoth in their magic, that doesn't make you a Nephandi.<br /> <br /> Likewise, there's a big difference between using the idea of Cthulhu in your occultism and actually having Cthulhu show up in your setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T15:04:04-07:00","id":1298197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1297008-qlippothic-spheres-and-non-nephandi?p=1297706#post1297706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's using Qlippothic as a interesting label to talk about something. If you want to have a Hermetic or whoever to use the actual Qlippoth in their magic, that doesn't make you a Nephandi.<br /> <br /> Likewise, there's a big difference between using the idea of Cthulhu in your occultism and actually having Cthulhu show up in your setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>So... the hermetics are just being all metaphorical when they call the spheres sephiroth?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20546-dragonchild","name":"Dragonchild","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T15:47:54-07:00","id":1298206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dragonchild</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1297008-qlippothic-spheres-and-non-nephandi?p=1298197#post1298197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So... the hermetics are just being all metaphorical when they call the spheres sephiroth?</div> </div> </div> </div>Kinda. I mean, the problem is that the Sephiroth/Qlippoth are an element of a real spiritual practices, whilst the Hermetics and the Qlippothic spheres are not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T06:20:23-07:00","id":1298308,"title":"","content":"Tidbit: <i>Mage: The Ascencion Order of Hermes </i>is not a real life spiritual tradition, but hermeticism/hermetism IS a real life spiritual practice","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T15:28:16-07:00","id":1298409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1297008-qlippothic-spheres-and-non-nephandi?p=1298308#post1298308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tidbit: <i>Mage: The Ascencion Order of Hermes </i>is not a real life spiritual tradition, but hermeticism/hermetism IS a real life spiritual practice</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe I'm not being clear, that's precisely the distinction I'm making. The Hermetics and the Qlippothic Spheres are drawing on real life spiritual practice (ie. Hemeticism), but they're distinct enough that it actually creates problems.<br /> <br /> Like, Dragonchild mentioned RL occultism which uses the Qlippoth or the Tysonomicon, and my point is those rely to some extent on those concepts being somewhat <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">malleable</span></span></span>. However, for an Order of Hermes mage, the Qlippoth Spheres aren't malleable in that same way, they have a very concrete reality.<br /> <br /> There's a difference between a chaos magician using a paradigm based around the Cthulhu Mythos, and actually meeting Cthulhu as presented in the original story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T20:23:04-07:00","id":1298474,"title":"","content":"Back in the era of Mage 2nd edition, I had a character that was a reformed infernalist who'd made some bargains but gotten cold feet/come to his senses before actually taking the plunge. While I don't recall ever actually using Qlippothic magic in-game, he knew some Entropy effects in that style and his spells in general tended to have a scary/sinister vibe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}